From a501e10a90266f9f88ad847135a68945032d87c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Royna2544 <whiteshell2544@naver.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:22:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] coreboot: Quiesce the PICs before running a CBFS payload

cbfs_run_payload() jumped to the payload with the 8259s still at the
BIOS vector base 0x08, the BIOS IRQs (timer, keyboard, ...) unmasked
and possibly an interrupt request latched while SeaBIOS ran with
interrupts disabled. A payload that enables interrupts before taking
over the PICs, such as edk2's CpuDxe, then takes that request on an
exception vector, or as a spurious IRQ7 if the PICs were only masked.
On a Foxconn G31MX-K edk2 stopped with "X64 Exception Type - 0F" in
CpuDxe, and with "Type - 27" after only moving the vector base.

Before the jump, mask the PICs, let a latched request reach the BIOS
handlers through yield(), then reinitialise the PICs to vector bases
0x20/0x28, as coreboot leaves them, with all inputs masked.
---
 src/fw/coreboot.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/fw/coreboot.c b/src/fw/coreboot.c
index 7c0954b5..572fa859 100644
--- a/src/fw/coreboot.c
+++ b/src/fw/coreboot.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include "config.h" // CONFIG_*
 #include "e820map.h" // e820_add
 #include "hw/pcidevice.h" // pci_probe_devices
+#include "hw/pic.h" // pic_irqmask_write
 #include "lzmadecode.h" // LzmaDecode
 #include "malloc.h" // free
 #include "output.h" // dprintf
@@ -519,6 +520,15 @@ cbfs_run_payload(struct cbfs_file *fhdr)
             break;
         case PAYLOAD_SEGMENT_ENTRY: {
             dprintf(1, "Calling addr %p\n", dest);
+            // The payload sets up its own interrupt handling. Mask the PICs
+            // and let an interrupt request that is already latched reach
+            // the BIOS handlers (as spurious IRQ7), so the payload does not
+            // take it when it first enables interrupts. Then move the PICs
+            // off the exception vectors, as coreboot leaves them.
+            pic_irqmask_write(0xffff);
+            yield();
+            pic_reset(0x20, 0x28);
+            pic_irqmask_write(0xffff);
             void (*func)(void) = dest;
             func();
             return;
-- 
2.56.0

